{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 106, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a weak avg_pool with an identity shortcut gains much more (+3.6 to +9) than replacing a conv op (#17, #30, #92 vs #59)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Connecting a previously removed input edge with a 3x3 conv gives huge gains (#5, #69), versus small changes when swapping existing ops."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping avg_pool for a 3x3 conv on edge 2 improves accuracy (#63, #97), more than when it replaces other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to a missing output edge gives larger gains than refining an existing conv (#19, #40 vs #16, #82)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing avg_pool on edge 1 with a 1x1 conv helps consistently (#67), more than replacing none (#74)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading avg_pool to 3x3 conv on edge 4 gains on all datasets (#18, #41), unlike upgrades from skip (#49)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a harmful avg_pool on edge 3 helps (#1), whereas removing a conv on edge 3 hurts (#7, #15, #43)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Putting avg_pool onto a removed edge 1 costs much more (#35) than swapping it for conv or skip ops (#38, #62)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "